    <p>The recap also teased a Furbolg city dungeon in the same family as these destinations (per Inven Global's coverage, which names the Timbermaw Hold dungeon). Beta-era dungeon data (classicwowforever, September 17) reads that furbolg city as <strong>Blackmaw Hold in Azshara</strong> — behind the furbolg gates — with no separate Timbermaw Hold record found. Dungeon quests and new rewards are planned to keep running content part of Forever's loop. Themes above follow Blizzard's Forever panel videos (transcribed by wowforeverclassic, September 17); no outlet has disclosed boss lists or Blueprint drops for any of the nine.</p>
    <p class="meta-info">Bracket caveats from wowforeverclassic's September 17 reads: Alcaz Prison's 48-53 range is graded only "reported" (no Blizzard source found), and its Krol'dok entry still shows the pre-correction 40-55 range (with a flagged 35-40 conflict) — the table retains the old range despite its September 17 check date, so the 40-45 correction stands.</p>
    <p class="meta-info">Beta-client captures (September 16, via Icy Veins) add unannounced instance maps beyond these nine: Dalaran City, Hyjal Crater, Warsong Gulch (Winter), Battle for Gilneas, "Half-Pint Tavern", "Manor Mistmantle" (sic), "Eastern Kingdoms Preserved", Azshara Crater, Karazhan Crypts, Shadow Hold, Storm Cliffs, Starfall Barrow Den, The Crystal Vale and a Scarab Dais / Searing Basin / Tainted Scar cluster. Presence in data does not mean shipping — classic and Season of Discovery maps appear throughout the same files, and Blizzard has announced none of these (datamined, unconfirmed). The "Dalaran City" map most likely corresponds to the open-world Dalaran city above (per wowforeverclassic.com's reading), not a hidden instance.</p>
