    </ul>
    <h3>Racial redesigns worth noting</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>Dwarf</strong> (Blizzard-confirmed) — <strong>Stoneform</strong> removes Bleeds, Poisons and Diseases, grants immunity to them and reduces Physical damage taken by 10% for 8 seconds (3-min cooldown) instead of increasing Armor; <strong>Find Treasure</strong> becomes an active that tracks treasure chests on the minimap and can stay on alongside other tracking; new passives <strong>Mace Specialization</strong> (+1% spell and ability crit with a mace equipped) and <strong>Big Game Hunter</strong> (+5% damage to beasts)</li>
        <li><strong>Undead</strong> (Blizzard-confirmed) — <strong>Will of the Forsaken</strong> breaks Charm, Fear and Sleep on a 2-minute cooldown but no longer grants immunity; <strong>Cannibalize</strong> now restores Mana as well as Health (7% of each every 2s for 10s); <strong>Touch of the Grave</strong> drains up to 5% of max Health on a 5% proc chance; Underwater Breathing (300% longer) unchanged</li>
        <li><strong>Troll</strong> (Blizzard-confirmed, from the in-game race selection screen) — <strong>Berserking</strong> flattened to a flat 10% attack/casting speed for 10s (no longer scaling 10-30% with missing health); <strong>Rapid Regeneration</strong> restores 50% of max Health over a short period; Beast Slaying and +10% health regeneration unchanged</li>
        <li><strong>Human</strong> (verified across reports) — <strong>Will to Survive</strong> breaks all Stuns; <strong>Perception</strong> detects stealthed enemies for 20s; <strong>Sword Specialization</strong> becomes +2% spell/ability crit with swords (weapon-skill bonus dropped); The Human Spirit +5% Spirit unchanged; Diplomacy dropped</li>
        <li><strong>Orc</strong> (verified) — <strong>Shatter Curse</strong> new: 8s immunity to Curses, plus reduced magic damage taken; <strong>Blood Fury</strong> now +10% Attack/Spell Power for 15s with no healing penalty mentioned; <strong>Hardiness</strong> reduces stun durations by 20% (was a chance to resist); <strong>Axe Specialization</strong> +1% crit; Command (+5% pet damage) dropped</li>
        <li><strong>Gnome</strong> (verified) — <strong>Eureka!</strong> new: next 3 spells/abilities cost less and deal 10% more damage or healing; <strong>Escape Artist</strong> breaks roots/snares with a brief immunity (one report: 5s); <strong>Expansive Mind</strong> now +5% max Mana, Rage and Energy (was +5% Intellect); Engineering Specialization resolved for reliability: more reliable devices (per Blizzard article 24304075)</li>
        <li><strong>Tauren</strong> (verified) — <strong>Plainsrunning</strong> new: movement speed builds as you keep moving (no numbers yet); <strong>Cultivation</strong> grows bonus herb nodes around you that anyone can gather without Herbalism; <strong>War Stomp</strong> 2s stun on up to 5 enemies within 8 yards; <strong>Endurance</strong> +5% health and +1% hit chance</li>
        <li><strong>Night Elf</strong> (verified) — <strong>Elune's Light</strong> new: +10% critical strike for 15s; <strong>Wisp Spirit</strong> movement speed while dead up to +75%; Quickness resolved at 1% dodge + 2% run speed (per Blizzard article 24304075)</li>
        <li><strong>Racial structure</strong> — each race now has two active and two passive abilities, tuned to deliver similar offensive power while preserving signature utility (per the Deep Dive recap)</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-info">Racial tooltips captured from the September 12 pre-release build per classicwowforever.com; Dwarf, Undead and Troll entries above are Blizzard-confirmed reads (per wowforeverclassic's Official-grade pages, sourced to the Deep Dive recap and the in-game race selection screen), while Human/Night Elf/Gnome/Orc/Tauren rest on 2-3 independent reports (their "verified" grade). Night Elf Quickness (1% dodge + 2% run speed) and Gnome Engineering Specialization (device reliability) are resolved official per Blizzard article 24304075 (September 22). Command and Diplomacy are dropped — wowforeverclassic's full racials table (40 racials: 17 new, 15 changed, each graded with sources) lists neither for any race — and the Classic weapon-skill specializations became crit-based (Sword +2%, Axe +1%, Mace +1% spell-and-ability crit). Pre-release values can change before launch.</p>
</section>

<section class="panel cp-span-full">
    <h2>Legacy, Camping and How Legacy Points Work</h2>
    <p>Legacy is Forever's account-wide progression layer, delivered through perk trees rather than traditional account systems. Per the official Forever overview and classicwowforever.com's Legacy guide (September 13, 2026), the model breaks into three parts: earn points via first-time challenges, spend points on perks per character, and work the collection track.</p>
    <h3>The points economy (per classicwowforever.com's review of the pre-release build)</h3>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>Earn up to 65 Legacy points at launch</strong>, shared across your alts</li>
        <li><strong>Each character can spend up to 16 points</strong> across all three perk trees; every character picks its own allocation</li>
        <li>Points come from first-time <strong>Legacy Challenges</strong>: class milestones, tradeskills, quests, exploration, PvP ranks and dungeon/raid goals</li>
        <li>Hardcore progression stays separate: Hardcore accomplishments can flow out to other rulesets, but other rulesets' progress does not flow back in (per the Deep Dive recap and the Legacy guide); wowforeverclassic (official) adds that Hardcore is excluded from account-wide Collections and Legacy Points</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Challenge examples observed in the pre-release build</h3>
    <table class="fact-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Challenge type</th><th scope="col">Observed milestones (1 point each, first-time)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Class (Druid, Warrior shown)</td><td>Level 25 · 45 · 60</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Profession (Engineering, Blacksmithing shown)</td><td>Skill 150 · 225 · 300</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Quests</td><td>Lord Valthalak Laid to Rest questline; Explore Azeroth achievement</td></tr>
            <tr><td>PvP ranks</td><td>Ranks 3, 7, 10, 13 and 14</td></tr>
            <tr><td>PvP season</td><td>Field of Honor journey, weeks 4, 7 and 10</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Dungeons</td><td>Novice / Experienced / Master Spelunker (dungeon lists collapsed in capture)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Raids</td><td>Conqueror of the Lair (defeat Onyxia) · Conquerer of the Wilds (Hyjal Summit) · Conquerer of the Deeps (Barrow Deeps)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Beta-client reads (classicwowforever, September 19) fill in the structure: the 65 break down as 27 class milestones, 18 crafting, 5 PvP ranks (3, 7, 10, 13, 14 only), 3 Field of Honor weeks, 4 battleground exalted, 3 dungeon sets, 3 raids and 2 exploration — with no challenges for gathering, Cooking, Fishing or First Aid. Trees gate deeper perks behind 5- and 10-point spend with left-connector prerequisites, 6 tree slots read "Not yet implemented" (2 per tree), and Legacy appears to open at level 25 (opening it earlier throws errors in beta, which is capped at 20).</p>
    <h3>The collection track (per Blizzard's reveal image)</h3>
    <table class="fact-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Points earned</th><th scope="col">Reward</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>15</td><td>Replica Ironforge Air Rifle</td></tr>
            <tr><td>25</td><td>Spectral Bear Cub (pet)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>40</td><td>Spectral Bear Tabard</td></tr>
            <tr><td>55</td><td>Reins of the Spectral Bear (mount)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Collected rewards are claimed from <strong>Innkeeper Wiley in Ratchet</strong> (per captured tooltips; the mount's claim location was not captured). Rewards sit on a separate track from perk spending, so challenges beyond the 16-point cap keep feeding the collection.</p>
    <div class="cp-cols">
        <div>
            <h3>Adventure</h3>
            <ul class="plain-list">
                <li><strong>Talented</strong> (Rank 0/5) — talent points start at level 9 instead of 10 (still capped at 51)</li>
                <li><strong>Well Rested</strong> (Rank 0/5) — rested XP accumulates 4% faster, cap +4%</li>
                <li><strong>Thrill of Adventure</strong> (Rank 0/5) — killing blows restore 1% max Health/Mana over 10s; disabled in dungeons, raids and battlegrounds</li>
