<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="roadmap">
    <h2>The Content Roadmap</h2>
    <p>Blizzard's roadmap positions Forever as a long-lived, evergreen product that keeps expanding the original world over time. The 2026–27 plan below comes from Blizzard's official roadmap graphic and the 2026–2027 roadmap pinned post on the official forums (transcribed by classicwowforever.com where fine print was only legible in-capture).</p>
    <img src="https://bnetcmsus-a.akamaihd.net/cms/content_entry_media/u5/U52GZGEAYVPB1789248906010.png" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" alt="World of Warcraft: Forever roadmap 2026-2027" class="img-round">
    <ul class="news-list">
        <li><time>Sep 17 – Oct 21 2026</time> Beta (level 20 cap at start, rising to 30 after a couple of weeks, per Icy-Veins; access via Epic/Collection). Closing date read as October 21 in purchase terms and October 22 on the roadmap graphic, with Warcraft Tavern's September 17 beta guide and classicwowforever's access reference also reading October 22 — discrepancy not yet resolved. Beta went live September 17; Blizzard posted the first known-issues list the same day</li>
        <li><time>Sep 17 2026</time> Live Q&A — two segments: modern WoW 10:00 a.m. PT, Forever at 10:30 a.m. PT (18:30 BST / 17:30 UTC), per Blizzard's [watch post](https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24302544/watch-the-world-of-warcraft-live-q-a-september-17); official Warcraft Twitch and YouTube (VOD after). Questions via forums: <a href="https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/submit-your-question-for-the-live-wow-qa-on-september-17/2347251">NA thread</a> / <a href="https://eu.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/world-of-warcraft-live-qa-september-17/628062">EU thread</a>; Retail and Forever questions both welcome</li>
        <li><time>Oct 20 2026</time> Invite-A-Friend codes begin arriving by email</li>
        <li><time>Oct 27 – Nov 3 2026</time> Early Name Reservation, up to three characters, first-come-first-served</li>
        <li><time>Nov 4 2026</time> Global launch, 3:00 p.m. PST — four new regions, nine dungeons, Darkspear Islands, and endgame encounters opening at the Barrow Deeps and Hyjal Summit (raids unlock December 9)</li>
        <li><time>Dec 9 2026</time> First raids unlock — Hyjal Summit (20-player) and the Barrow Deeps (10-player); Onyxia's Lair (40-player) named by Zierhut as the third raid with tier pieces across all three, Dec 9 date per roadmap transcription [Dec 9 timing NEEDS VERIFICATION]. A second independent fan read (wowforeverclassic.com, graded "reported") also places Onyxia on December 9, from the roadmap slide. New tier sets and the legendary reward accompany them</li>
        <li><time>Winter 2026-27</time> <strong>Hardcore</strong> planned for Forever, available after launch with a death-transfer path to other rulesets (no date or full rule set yet). Zierhut told The Sun it is "coming next year," with the team wanting bugs worked out first: "You don't want people dying because they ran into a bug"</li>
        <li><time>Spring 2027</time> Two raids (10 and 20-player), two dungeons, more quests and playable area, a legendary questline, and a PvP refresh</li>
        <li><time>Summer 2027</time> A revamped iconic raid, another raid, two dungeons, expanded world content, plus PvP, profession and Legacy updates</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta-info">Roadmap per Blizzard's official roadmap graphic and forums post, September 12 2026; dates corroborated by Blizzard's official What's Next and Deep Dive recaps (September 12-13 2026). Spring/Summer 2027 details transcribed from the roadmap capture by classicwowforever.com. Longer-term items are subject to change.</p>
</section>

