<section class="panel cp-span-full" id="faq">
    <h2>World of Warcraft: Forever FAQ</h2>
    <ul class="plain-list">
        <li><strong>What is World of Warcraft: Forever?</strong> The official Classic+ product announced at BlizzCon 2026 — a permanent, evergreen version of original Azeroth being expanded by the Classic team. It is not a mode, a season, or a new version of Classic; it is a third WoW experience beside Modern and Classic.</li>
        <li><strong>When is WoW: Forever's release date?</strong> November 4, 2026 at 3:00 p.m. PST. First new raids follow on December 9, 2026. Beta begins September 17, 2026.</li>
        <li><strong>Is Forever free, or does it cost money?</strong> It is included with an active WoW subscription or game time — no separate purchase is required to play outside of the optional Skyborne upgrade packs. The Skyborne Heroic Pack (launch price independently reported at $29.99/€29.99), Skyborne Epic Pack (adds beta access and 30 days game time), and Warcraft Forever Collection (adds Warcraft III Reforged: Forsaken Kingdom, available through January 11 2027) are the only paid editions.</li>
        <li><strong>Is the Skyborne race free?</strong> No. Per Blizzard's official pre-purchase announcement, the Skyborne race and their Zephras Isle starting experience are part of the paid Skyborne Heroic Pack and above. Race access is the one gap in otherwise sub-only Forever content.</li>
        <li><strong>Is Forever beta free?</strong> The guaranteed beta route requires an upgrade purchase — access comes with the Skyborne Epic Pack and Warcraft Forever Collection. GameSpot also lists a free opt-in on the WoW Forever website, described as a signup that does not guarantee a seat. Independent coverage reports the beta itself will not require a subscription or game time, and that beta leveling is capped at 30 (both [NEEDS VERIFICATION]). The beta runs September 17 through October 21, 2026. Beta-ops notes (wowforeverclassic, per Blizzard's support article): the beta client can go offline at any time, and there are no separate beta forums — feedback goes to the WoW Forever forum.</li>
        <li><strong>Will Forever stay at level 60?</strong> Yes — Blizzard confirmed the cap is "will always be" 60, with raids, dungeons and world content expanding the endgame rather than raising the cap.</li>
        <li><strong>Is Classic+ coming, or was that just a codename?</strong> Classic+ is now official as World of Warcraft: Forever. The Project Camelot codename and encrypted Patch 1.60 builds tracked here led directly to this product; see the Project Camelot timeline above.</li>
        <li><strong>What zones does Forever add?</strong> Mount Hyjal and Shen'dralas in Kalimdor, the Riverglades in the Eastern Kingdoms, and Zephras Isle (the Skyborne starting zone), plus expanded and reimagined existing areas and over 1,000 new quests across levels 1–60.</li>
        <li><strong>Where can I play Classic+-style content today?</strong> Private servers fill the gap until Forever launches — see our ranked picks in <a href="/blog/best-vanilla-plus-private-servers-2026/">the best Vanilla+ servers of 2026</a> or browse the full <a href="/">server tracker</a>.</li>
    </ul>
